      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Given that the center of the circle is on the $x$-axis, we can assume the relationship $B\\left(x, 0\\right)$ where $x$ is the $x$ coordinate of the center. Using the distance formula, we can set up the equation $\\sqrt{\\left(x-1\\right)^{2}+\\left(0-3\\right)^{2}}=\\sqrt{(x-0)^{2}+4^{2}}$. Solving for $x$, we find $x=5$. Therefore, the radius of the circle is $\\sqrt{5^2+4^2}=\\boxed{3\\sqrt{5}}.$",
