      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The center of the circle is directly above or below one of the points.\nLet the coordinates of the center be $(c,0)$ and let the radius be $r$.\nThe distance from $(0,4)$ to $(c,0)$ is $\\sqrt{((0-c)^2 + (4-0)^2)}= \\sqrt{(c^2 - 2c + 16)}$.\nThe distance from $(1,3)$ to $(c,0)$ is $\\sqrt{((1-c)^2 + (3-0)^2)}= \\sqrt{(c^2 - 2c + 10)}$.\nSince these distances are equal (both are radius of the circle), we have the equation: $$\n\\sqrt{c^2 - 2c + 16}= \\sqrt{c^2 - 2c + 10}\n$$\nBy squaring both sides, we get: $$\nc^2 - 2c + 16= c^2 - 2c + 10\n$$\nSetting them equal to each other, we get $$\n\\begin{align*}\nc^2 - 2c + 16 &= c^2 - 2c + 10 \\\\\n16 &= 10 \\\\\n6 &= 0\n\\end{align*}\n$$\nTherefore, the radius of the circle is $7$.",
